{"name":"Card Table Green","hex":"#00512c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"card","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["cardinality"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A playing card.","Any game using playing cards; a card game."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/card"},{"term":"table","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Furniture with a top surface to accommodate a variety of uses.","An item of furniture with a flat top surface raised above the ground, usually on one or more legs."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To tabulate; to put into a table or grid. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To supply (a guest, client etc.) with food at a table; to feed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/table"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Folding table","blocks":[{"text":"A folding table is a type of folding furniture, a table with legs that fold up against the table top. This is intended to make storage more convenient and to make the table more portable. Many folding tables are made of lightweight materials to further increase portability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Folding_table.jpg/330px-Folding_table.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folding_table","wikidata":"Q5464307"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/16CenturyFoldingTable.png/330px-16CenturyFoldingTable.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/16CenturyFoldingTable.png/330px-16CenturyFoldingTable.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 16th-century English folding table","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A16CenturyFoldingTable.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/RollsRoyceTAble.jpg/500px-RollsRoyceTAble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/RollsRoyceTAble.jpg/1280px-RollsRoyceTAble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/RollsRoyceTAble.jpg/500px-RollsRoyceTAble.jpg?utm_sourc